From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Open Arc Authors <dev@openarc.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 19:32:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] openarc: embedder: keep //chrome without its UI

Plan C6b (decision Q7): the embedder moves from content level to
//chrome.

- OpenArcMainDelegate derives from ChromeMainDelegate (compiled into
  //openarc:embedder with Chrome's crash reporter client, as
  //chrome:chrome_dll does for Chrome's framework); the hang watcher is
  off because the browser's main thread is the shell app's.
- OpenArcContentBrowserClient derives from ChromeContentBrowserClient
  and keeps Chrome's dialogs out: no Chrome context menu view delegate,
  no client-certificate picker, no login prompt, no external-protocol
  dialog (default answers until C12), and the shell's per-tab color
  scheme wins over Chrome's.
- OpenArcBrowserMainExtraParts: our keychain item name ("Open Arc Safe
  Storage"), default prefs (Safe Browsing off, sign-in off, background
  mode off) and closing every tab before Chrome destroys profiles.
- OACApplication puts Chrome in its embedder-owned-UI mode (no Chrome
  window, menu, status item or startup browser), passes
  --user-data-dir and Open Arc's default switches (no first run,
  default-browser check, sync, component updates), and loads profiles
  through ProfileManager at <userDataDirectory>/<UUID>.
- OACProfile wraps a Chrome Profile (with a profile keep-alive) and its
  primary off-the-record profile.
- OACTab attaches //chrome's tab helpers (openarc::TabHelpersAccess) and
  reports favicons from ContentFaviconDriver; the favicon change is now
  detected (C9 request 1) and cleared on cross-document navigations.
  Permission prompts are dismissed until C12.
- The framework bundles Chrome's resource packs and the crashpad
  handler instead of openarc.pak.
- openarc_shell_test logs NSApp, its delegate, windows and menu, the
  title and favicon before --quit-after-load quits.
